WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.485 --> 00:00:02.070
(gun fires)

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.930
- [Narrator] In June, Ukraine began

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.104
its long awaited counter-offensive.

00:00:06.104 --> 00:00:07.230
(rocket fires)

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.540
The hope then was that Ukrainian soldiers

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.330
equipped with modern Western
weapons would recapture

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.347
territory taken by the Russians.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.500
(rocket fires)

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.030
But that plan has not worked.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.330
Despite breaches of Russian
defenses near Robotyne,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.400
Ukraine has liberated just a fraction

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.310
of the territory that
Russia occupied in June.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.170
- Ukraine is a long way from achieving

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.360
a big and significant breakthrough.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.220
- The counter offensive up to this point

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.641
has been disappointing
both for the Ukrainians

00:00:34.641 --> 00:00:36.183
and for the West.

00:00:37.372 --> 00:00:39.060
(explosives fire)

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.130
- [Narrator] But recently,
things have been going better

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.840
for Ukraine elsewhere.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.850
After ramping up missile and drone strikes

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.871
on the Crimean Peninsula, the
important Russian supply route

00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:50.700
over the Kerch Bridge was disrupted,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.550
and Russia was forced to
withdraw its Black Sea Fleet

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.259
from its base in Sevastopol.

00:00:56.259 --> 00:00:57.092
(rocket fires)

00:00:57.092 --> 00:00:58.935
Now, with winter approaching,

00:00:58.935 --> 00:00:59.970
(rocket fires)

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.390
focus has turned to what's
next for the biggest war

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.377
on European soil in nearly eight decades.

00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:08.151
(gun fires)

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:09.660
(piano music)

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.310
- So what are we seeing right now?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:16.050
Slow movement near Bakhmut,
Robotyne, and Kherson.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.460
- [Narrator] Mark Kimmitt is retired

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.710
US Army Brigadier General who served

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.560
in Bosnia, Kosovo, and Iraq.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.057
- They are continuing
their ground offensive

00:01:25.057 --> 00:01:29.632
to try to reach down into the Sea of Asov.

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:34.415
Mariupol is probably the
target for this northern axis.

00:01:34.415 --> 00:01:38.055
Berdiansk, Melitopol, the center axis,

00:01:38.055 --> 00:01:40.268
and from Kherson, of course,

00:01:40.268 --> 00:01:45.268
cutting off the Crimean
Bridge, the Crimean Peninsula

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.200
from Donbas, what we call
cutting the land bridge.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.860
The Russians, by contrast,
they are continuing to defend

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.053
along these lines and
their number one objective

00:01:58.053 --> 00:02:02.633
is to hold those lines
as long as they can,

00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:05.850
but while they're using
their ground forces to go

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.610
against either defend or counter attack

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.640
against the Ukrainian
forces, they're also using

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.095
their long range missiles
to attack civilian targets.

00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:19.290
(foreign language)

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.363
Here, military targets.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.860
Here, civilian and infrastructure targets.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.070
So the Russians are truly
fighting a total war

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:32.460
against soldiers and
against the civilians.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.570
- [Narrator] While progress in the north

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.250
of the country has been slow-going,

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.937
General Kimmitt believes the Ukrainians

00:02:36.937 --> 00:02:40.320
have recently seen more success in Crimea.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.020
- They've started attacking
down here in Crimea

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.700
where here they've been trying
to fight ground maneuver

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.620
to take ground and get to the sea of Asov.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:53.340
Down here, it's more of
a air and naval fight.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.580
If you take a look at the targets,

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.350
they've been attacking Sevastopol,

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:03.350
which is the headquarters of
the Russian Black Sea Fleet.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:07.133
They've also been attacking
the airfield of Saky,

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:10.113
the air defense sites of Yevpatoriya,

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.780
and also in the Boyko oil
platforms and radar platforms

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.900
that they have out in the Black Sea.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.300
Kerch Bridge, you knock that out,

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.330
you stop the logistics flow into Crimea.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.361
You take out that bridge and
you're forced to resupply

00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:33.360
by sea and by air, and
that's very, very tough.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.760
You can't get the quantities of material

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.980
to support the types of artillery war

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.540
that the Russians are fighting.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.300
- This bridge will
certainly continue to be

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.970
a major target for Ukraine in this war.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.042
One of the difficulties
with defending the bridge

00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:50.760
is the variety of the attacks
that the Ukrainians have used

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.578
against it and the different
options that they have.

00:03:53.578 --> 00:03:56.400
First of all, they've used a truck bomb.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.590
Second, they used naval drones.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.530
There's also a possibility
that if their forces

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.200
in the southeast of the
country are able to drive

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.522
further south, they will
put the bridge in range

00:04:07.522 --> 00:04:10.170
of the missiles that Ukraine has.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.541
Ukraine is also asking the
West for further missiles

00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:15.720
which have a longer range

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.918
and would therefore be
able to strike the bridge.

00:04:17.918 --> 00:04:19.620
(missile roars)

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.410
- [Narrator] In September,
President Biden said the US

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.536
is willing to provide advanced long range

00:04:24.536 --> 00:04:27.180
surface to surface ATACMS missiles

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.520
to help Kiev with its counter-offensive.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.890
- I believe bringing in the ATACMS

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.975
will make a tremendous difference.

00:04:33.975 --> 00:04:36.090
The longest range weapons system

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.950
that the Ukrainians have right now

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.740
are their own rockets and HIMARS.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.480
This line, this little bar,

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.800
represents about a hundred
kilometers, 60 miles.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.898
That's the range of the HIMARS.

00:04:49.898 --> 00:04:54.898
It's usually doctrine that
you put your artillery

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.240
and your missiles about one third

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:01.380
of the way behind the front lines.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.635
So in this case, you would see

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:06.570
that in all of these formations,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.290
in all these attack routes,
you can reach to some

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:15.290
but not all of the Russian
attack areas and rear areas.

00:05:16.578 --> 00:05:20.254
When you bring in the
ATACMS, everything changes.

00:05:20.254 --> 00:05:22.470
(missile roars)

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.100
It has a range of about 300 kilometers

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.470
and has no problem reaching

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:32.910
all of the ground in those attack routes.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.636
So all of the logistics,
all of the command posts,

00:05:35.636 --> 00:05:40.530
all of the resupply dumps are in peril

00:05:41.716 --> 00:05:46.050
and as importantly, so is Crimea.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:51.050
You can see that if you
bring the HIMARS close enough

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.216
to the front line and you
bring the ATACMS ammunition,

00:05:56.216 --> 00:06:00.450
you can generally reach
everything in Crimea.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.760
- [Narrator] Recently,
Russia withdrew the bulk

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.550
of its Black Sea Fleet
from its main Crimean base

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.639
in Sevastopol, following a series

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:10.800
of drone and missile strikes by Ukraine.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.500
- Ukraine, to all intents and
purposes, does not have a Navy

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.380
and so it's all the more astonishing

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.460
that they have been able
to launch attacks on Russia

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.377
which has one of its most powerful fleets

00:06:22.377 --> 00:06:24.660
based in Sevastopol.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.740
Ukraine has already managed
to sink its flagship

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.221
and constantly carries out
attacks on other boats.

00:06:33.221 --> 00:06:34.054
(foreign language)

00:06:34.054 --> 00:06:35.730
- [Narrator] Going
forward, General Kimmitt

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.590
sees three potential options.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:41.340
- I think the three options
for the counter-offensive

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.255
before we go into the fighting season,

00:06:43.255 --> 00:06:48.255
are that the Ukrainians
achieve some breakthrough.

00:06:48.599 --> 00:06:50.850
(gun fires)

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.920
And they will try to then break out,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.400
perhaps get all the way through a area

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.630
of the defensive lines

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:01.710
and pour as many troops through
that formation as possible.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:05.880
I think the second option would simply be

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:10.060
that we are where we are as
we settle into the winter

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.924
and the formations,
either on the Russian side

00:07:14.924 --> 00:07:19.806
or the Ukrainian sides,
have local counter attacks

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:23.790
but don't make a significant
amount of progress.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.480
The third option, which I
think is the most unlikely,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.143
is that the additional
equipment that is brought in

00:07:31.143 --> 00:07:36.143
by the west and the fact that we are now

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:41.540
in somewhat of a battle of
exhaustion may cause a rethinking

00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:45.180
of the purpose of this war,

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.520
and it could very well
be that the Ukrainians

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.781
are pushed to begin
diplomatic negotiations.

00:07:51.781 --> 00:07:54.630
- [Narrator] Last July,
General Kimmitt wrote

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:59.245
a WSJ editorial about what he
saw as the most likely option.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.200
(gun fires)

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.200
- At that time, I believed
that the war would eventually

00:08:06.763 --> 00:08:11.763
reach this type of World War I stalemate

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.140
and trench warfare, artillery warfare.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.140
Unfortunately, I was right
and I stand by my conclusion

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.600
that not only will this
be the case in 2023

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.322
but could very well be the case in 2024.

00:08:27.322 --> 00:08:30.239
(foreign language)

00:08:32.421 --> 00:08:34.921
(tense music)

